diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..cafa1d4 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -116,6 +116,68 @@ HTTP/1.1 201 Created
 
 Returns the reactivated webhook in the response body.
 
+## Deliveries
+
+When an event a webhook is subscribed to happens on its board, Fizzy makes exactly one `POST` to the payload URL. A delivery is never retried: if the receiver is down or answers with an error, the delivery is logged as failed and the next event gets its own, separate delivery.
+
+__Request headers:__
+
+| Header | Value |
+| --- | --- |
+| `User-Agent` | `fizzy/1.0.0 Webhook` |
+| `Content-Type` | `application/json` (`text/html` for Campfire) |
+| `X-Webhook-Timestamp` | When the request was made, in ISO 8601 (e.g. `2025-12-05T19:36:35.401Z`) |
+| `X-Webhook-Signature` | Hex-encoded HMAC-SHA256 of the request body, keyed with the webhook's `signing_secret` |
+
+Verify a request came from Fizzy by computing the HMAC yourself and comparing it to the signature:
+
+```ruby
+expected = OpenSSL::HMAC.hexdigest("SHA256", signing_secret, request.body.read)
+ActiveSupport::SecurityUtils.secure_compare(expected, request.headers["X-Webhook-Signature"])
+```
+
+__Request body:__
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohde",
+  "action": "card_closed",
+  "created_at": "2025-12-05T19:36:35.401Z",
+  "eventable": {
+    "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohdb",
+    "number": 1,
+    "title": "Fix the login page",
+    "status": "published",
+    "url": "http://app.fizzy.localhost:3006/897362094/cards/1",
+    ...
+  },
+  "board": {
+    "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohcy",
+    "name": "Fizzy",
+    ...
+  },
+  "creator": {
+    "id": "03f5v9zjw7pz8717a4no1h8a7",
+    "name": "David Heinemeier Hansson",
+    ...
+  }
+}
+```
+
+`eventable` is the card or comment the event is about, in the same shape as the [Cards](cards.md) and [Comments](comments.md) endpoints return them.
+
+Payload URLs pointing at chat services get a ready-to-post message instead:
+
+- Slack incoming webhooks (`https://hooks.slack.com/services/…`) receive `{ "text": "…" }`.
+- Campfire bots (`…/rooms/:room_id/:bot_key/messages`) receive the message as HTML.
+- Basecamp Campfire chatbots (`…/integrations/:key/buckets/:bucket_id/chats/:chat_id/lines`) receive `{ "content": "<html>" }`.
+
+__Failures and deactivation:__
+
+A delivery counts as successful when the receiver answers with a `2xx` status. Anything else—another status, a timeout, or an unreachable host—counts as a failure. A webhook that fails ten deliveries in a row over the course of an hour is switched off (`"active": false`) and stops receiving deliveries until it's reactivated via the activation endpoint above, which also clears its failure streak.
+
+Deliveries are kept in the log for a week.
+
 ## `GET /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/webhooks/:webhook_id/deliveries`
 
 Returns a paginated list of deliveries for a webhook. Only account admins can access delivery history.
